     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, the usual analgesic dosing\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
